The source is revealing: `fread(buf, 1, sizeof(buf), f)` caps reads at 64 bytes, so `n` can never exceed 64 — meaning `if (n > 999) abort();` looks unreachable. Let me post my intro, then verify this empirically before drawing conclusions.<action>
