</action>

As predicted, no crash — `fread` caps at 64 bytes so `n > 999` is unreachable via file size. Before concluding anything, let me verify my source matches the manifest hashes (to rule out a bait-and-switch between what I see and what's graded), and probe special file types (directories, device files, FIFOs) that might behave oddly.<action>
